  clock: 2  # 4157
  nonce: '4157'  # 4157
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES. Remedies (1), (3), (4) hold as written. Remedy (2)'s code fact holds, but its stated CONSEQUENCE is overstated (details below). Read-only check: no tests run, no verdict A/B.\n\nDrift in the citations:\n- The audit is docs/surveys/call-construct-value-family-audit.md (3858e02445). docs/audits/0019 is a different audit (backend-agreement-rust-aardvark-dns).\n- Axiom wording: axis_meta_keys.py:334-348 still reads \"Source-language call construct collapsed under ast_call apex\". It now also defends 'constructor' in prose (INV-kahig), but the amendment proposed in (1) has not been made.\n- Membership test: verify_claims.py:4371-4372, in method_starved_modules (def at 4248); module_kinds is built at 4308-4320. The test is unchanged since INV-soval (46ca2dc353).\n- IoPrimitive.kind is now the io-primitive-kind axis {function, method, attribute} (io_primitive_kinds.py, ADR-0059), not io_boundary.py:633. 'attribute' is not a call_construct value, so the overlap is still two coinciding tokens.\n- Emit sites: erlang.py:599 'macro' (still carries evidence_type=macro_expansion); rust.py:3212 'macro_body'; the denylist is still at test_axis_meta_keys.py:411 with the same 4 values, and there is no allowlist.\n- A value the item does not list: 'protocol', emitted at py.py:5944 (dd3b7cf0ee, 2026-09-06) and covered by the survey audit at its line 63. Emitted values found by grep: 12, of which 10 are off-axis.\n\nCorrection to (2)'s consequence. method_starved_modules does `if not modules: continue` (verify_claims.py:4352) for any language that has no method-kind catalogue module. Measured with load_catalog(): elixir, erlang, haskell, ocaml, dart, csharp and ruby have 0 method-kind modules each. So for pipe, local, remote, application, monadic_action and dart/csharp 'constructor', the first route is never reached at all. There is no degradation there. Only these off-axis values reach the test:\n- python 'protocol', into django.db.models, which is a method-kind module through the community overlay;\n- js/ts 'assignment', whose dst is normally a local handler;\n- rust 'macro_body', whose dst is an in-repo target.\nWhether fixing (2) moves any verdict was NOT measured; the above makes \"inert\" the likely outcome to pre-register. The ZERO-consumers claim for macro/macro_body re-checked: no comparison against either value in packages/*/src.\n\nProposed item change: fix the audit path, and restate (2)'s consequence as \"reachable for python protocol / js assignment / rust macro_body only\"."  # 4157
