  set:  # cd70
    description: "FROM the call_construct value-family fundamental-concept audit of 2026-09-10\n(docs/surveys/call-construct-value-family-audit.md), which audits\n`Edge.meta[\"call_construct\"]`. Four remedies, in one item because they share a\nfile and a test.\n\nVALUES EMITTED TODAY (grep of packages/*/src): method, function, pipe, local,\nremote, application, monadic_action, macro, macro_body, constructor,\nassignment, protocol. Ten of the twelve are neither `function` nor `method`.\n\n(1) AMEND THE AXIOM. axis_meta_keys.py:334-348 says the key names the\n\"Source-language call construct\". Two shipped values are constructs that are\nNOT calls:\n  - `constructor`, which the registry prose itself defends: ruby emits `calls`\n    where dart/csharp emit `instantiates` for the same source construct\n    (INV-kahig);\n  - `assignment` (WI-dosuh: `ws.onmessage = h`).\nReword to \"Source-language construct that produced this call-family edge\". No\nvalue migration: the new wording is what the field has always meant. This is\nload-bearing, not cosmetic, because under the literal current wording\n`assignment` is off-axis.\n\n(2) FIX A CROSS-AXIS MEMBERSHIP TEST. In method_starved_modules\n(verify_claims.py:4248), at lines 4371-4372:\n\n    construct = (edge.get(\"meta\") or {}).get(\"call_construct\")\n    if construct and construct in module_kinds[language].get(module, set()):\n\n`module_kinds` (built at 4308-4320 from catalog.primitives) holds IoPrimitive.kind\nvalues. Those belong to the io-primitive-kind axis {function, method, attribute}\n(io_primitive_kinds.py, ADR-0059). So a call_construct value is\nmembership-tested against a DIFFERENT axis's value set, and the test works only\nbecause two tokens coincide.\n\nCONSEQUENCE, SCOPED. The function skips any language with no method-kind\ncatalogue module (`if not modules: continue`, line 4352). elixir, erlang,\nhaskell, ocaml, dart, csharp and ruby have none, so pipe, local, remote,\napplication, monadic_action and dart/csharp `constructor` never reach this\ntest. The off-axis values that DO reach it, and always fall through to the\nsecond (name) route whatever the module declares, are:\n  - python `protocol` (py.py:5944), into django.db.models, a method-kind module\n    through the community overlay;\n  - js/ts `assignment`, whose dst is normally a local handler;\n  - rust `macro_body`, whose dst is an in-repo target.\nNo error, no log line.\n\nNOT YET MEASURED: whether fixing it moves any verdict. The scope above makes\n\"inert\" the likely outcome; pre-register that, measure before and after on a\npython + js + rust cohort, and if it is inert say so rather than claiming a\nwin.\n\n(3) TURN THE DENYLIST INTO AN ALLOWLIST. test_axis_meta_keys.py:411 pins\n_FOLDED_CALL_CONSTRUCTS: four values previously ejected, with a positive\ncontrol proving the walk fires. That is the right guard for REGRESSION, but it\ncannot stop a value it has never seen. `assignment` shipped 2026-09-10 through\nevery gate in the repo with no review of whether it belongs on this axis.\nReplace the denylist with a declared allowlist, so that a new value must be\nadded deliberately. Keep the positive-control pattern.\n\n(4) MIGRATE THE TWO DEPRECATE-NO-FOLD VALUES.\n  - `macro` (erlang.py:599): the same edge already carries\n    evidence_type=\"macro_expansion\", so call_construct=macro restates the\n    inference pathway on a second axis. That is the exact rationale recorded\n    for ejecting `interface_dispatch`. Remove it; the fact already has a home.\n  - `macro_body` (rust.py:3212): names WHERE the call was found (inside a macro\n    token tree), not what it is. There is no uniform fold target, because\n    _extract_macro_call_names yields Self::-qualified, ::-qualified and bare\n    callees. Either stamp the real construct per site or stamp nothing.\nZERO consumers compare against either value, so this migration is\nproducer-only.\n\nORDERING NOTE: (3) should land AFTER (4), or the allowlist has to carry two\nvalues it is about to lose.\n\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # cd70
- op: discuss  # 6d0a
  at: '2026-10-01T09:07:26Z'  # 6d0a
  by: agent  # 6d0a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6d0a
  clock: 4  # 6d0a
  nonce: 6d0a  # 6d0a
  message: "EVIDENCE FROM WI-zohuk (2026-10-01, worktree ~/hg_wt/zohuk at dev 8cfcab7b07): remedy (2)'s \"js/ts assignment, whose dst is normally a local handler\" and its \"inert is the likely outcome\" are both refuted on a fixture, for the js member of the off-axis set.\n\nTHE DST IS THE CATALOGUE MODULE, NOT A LOCAL HANDLER. The handler-assignment edge (js_ts.py ~6138-6194) is emitted only when the receiver types to a catalogue module AND the property is a method-kind row of it, so its dst is e.g. javascript:WebSocket:0-0:onmessage, and io-boundaries classifies it (net_recv, WebSocket.onmessage). In method_starved_modules that edge (a) puts WebSocket in `called`, (b) fails route 1 because \"assignment\" is not in module_kinds[\"WebSocket\"] = {method}, and (c) fails route 2 because onmessage is a method-kind row, not a function-kind one. WebSocket is reported starved in the same run that classified a call into it.\n\nREPRO, two arms, survey + verify-claims (generic-taint-claims.yaml) per arm, arm A = HEAD with JS_ASSIGNABLE_ROWS emptied in an overlay copy (js_ts.py blob d8ca8124), arm B = HEAD (blob 11d17da8):\n  app.js:\n    function start(u, sink) {\n      const ws = new WebSocket(u);\n      ws.onmessage = function (ev) { console.log(ev.data); };\n      sink.write(\"x\");            // a method-stamped placeholder, so JS has construct evidence in BOTH arms\n    }\n  arm A: all 7 claims confirmed_with_caveats.\n  arm B: all 7 claims inconclusive, details \"NOT CONFIRMED: the analysis calls into 1 module(s) whose catalogued I/O is method-shaped (WebSocket) but produced no method call edge for any of them\".\nWithout the sink.write line the same flip happens for a second reason as well: the assignment edge is the first call_construct-bearing JS edge in the repo, so it also switches the gate's JS abstention off.\n\nCORPUS VOLUME (same A/B, cohort vscode, lila, nestjs, nest, argo-cd; nextjs pending at the time of writing): 0 verdict changes and 0 changed details strings. The flip needs a module reached ONLY through handler assignments and no satisfying method call; in every corpus repo that emits the construct (argo-cd production, nestjs/nest tests), the same receiver also has a method-stamped call (eventSource.close(), es.close()), which satisfies route 1. So corpus harm measured is 0, fixture harm is a verdict flip on every claim. Record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_09302026/zohuk/ (fx2_out is in the session scratchpad; the fixture is reproduced above).\n\nMinimal fix shape, NOT implemented here (out of WI-zohuk's scope): the satisfaction test needs to know that an \"assignment\" edge registers a METHOD-kind row (the emitter only stamps it on method-kind names), i.e. a construct-to-kind mapping instead of the raw membership test; that is remedy (2)'s axis fix. Also bears on WI-bobuf (this is a sixth classified-yet-starved instance)."  # 6d0a
- op: discuss  # e53a
  at: '2026-10-01T21:37:31Z'  # e53a
  by: agent  # e53a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e53a
  clock: 5  # e53a
  nonce: e53a  # e53a
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-01 (agent, worktree ~/hg_wt/dapap). Branch jgstern-agent/fix/dapap-call-construct-allowlist, commit 425771854b. Local only: not pushed, no PR, status unchanged.\n\nAll four remedies are implemented:\n(1) The axiom in axis_meta_keys now reads \"Source-language construct that produced this call-family edge\". The spec says the same.\n(2) method_starved_modules now translates call_construct through call_constructs.reached_row_kind, which gives the ADR-0059 kind of the row the construct reaches. It no longer tests the construct string for membership in the kind set. constructor and undeclared values map to None.\n(3) The new module hypergumbo_core/call_constructs.py declares CALL_CONSTRUCT_VALUES, 10 values, as an allowlist. It replaces the INV-tadup denylist; the folded values are kept as a \"never declare\" record that now also lists macro and macro_body. The emit scan now reads dict, keyword and subscript emits. The old scan read dict literals only, so it could not have seen 'assignment', which is a keyword emit. There is one positive control per shape. make_unresolved_edge raises on an undeclared value.\n(4) The erlang ?LOG_* edge and the rust macro-body edges no longer carry call_construct.\n\nEVIDENCE\n- Targeted smart-test: 22471 passed, 3 skipped, 5 xfailed, 0 failed, 685 test files, scoped coverage 100%, mypy ratchet clean.\n- Mutation check: putting the raw membership test back turns exactly 4 new tests red (assignment does-not-starve, coverage stays complete, assignment crosswalk, python protocol). The controls stay green: reach, method satisfies, and constructor / macro_body / bogus still starve.\n- End-to-end, on WI-zohuk's fixture (new WebSocket(u); ws.onmessage = fn; sink.write), with survey + verify-claims generic-taint-claims.yaml per arm and the verify_claims blob checked per arm:\n  - dev (blob 389cbef2ec97): 7/7 inconclusive, \"calls into 1 module(s) whose catalogued I/O is method-shaped (WebSocket) but produced no method call edge\".\n  - branch (blob 760abe557ca0): 7/7 confirmed_with_caveats.\n- Corpus: a gate-level A/B on six surveys gave 0 changes in the starved-module list. The dev gate and the branch gate ran on the same edge set; the branch arm also had the macro/macro_body stamps stripped, which is exactly what the branch's producers change. Off-axis edges into a method-kind module per survey:\n  - django (surveyed with this branch): 660 protocol edges.\n  - argo-cd: 1 assignment edge. nestjs: 2. nest: 2.\n  - lila: 0.\n  - ripgrep: 672 macro_body edges, none into a catalogued module.\n  The pre-registered \"inert on the corpus\" prediction holds on these six. It is refuted on the fixture, as WI-zohuk found. NOT measured: vscode (a 1.5 GB survey), and any repo where a django ORM module or WebSocket is reached ONLY through for-loops or handler assignments.\n\nNOT DONE, filed instead:\n- WI-pukip: rust per-site construct for macro-body calls, and the rust mis-stamp of resolved self.m() as 'function'. A method stamp moves unknown_receiver_scope's denominator, so this needs measuring first.\n- WI-dogid: register the vocabulary in audit_findings._REGISTRIES and move the survey to docs/audits.\n\nReport: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_09302026/dapap.md"  # e53a
